n\nRun one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after D0001. Expand at most one\neligible queued specification/catalogue chapter into no more than 250 `IMP-*`\nrecords, validate it, then allocate ready unassigned contracts into at most ten\nnew B-series authoring tasks with no more than seven R-series outputs each.\nCreate exactly one successor dispatcher when queued work or ready contracts\nremain; otherwise create exactly one final audit B-series task. Exit after that\nbounded set.\n\n## Context packet\n\nRead `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Review D0001's `dispatch_history` checkpoint and\nonly the canonical specification sections needed for a selected chapter.\n`SHARD-02` is not eligible until `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` is explicitly resolved;\n`SHARD-03` and `SHARD-04` retain their listed predecessor/gate blocks; and\n`SHARD-05` remains held unless explicit authorisation is recorded.\n\n## Output list\n\n- No R-series output is preassigned. Allocate R IDs only for ready, unassigned\n  catalogue contracts discovered after the bounded chapter check.\n- At most ten new B-series authoring runbooks, each owning no more than seven\n  newly assigned R-series outputs.\n- Exactly one successor dispatcher or one final audit B-series task, selected\n  only after the queue and ready-contract check.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nPreserve all accepted work and use monotonic B/R/IMP IDs. Do not infer approval\nfrom a gate or from a queued state. A selected expansion must include stable\nrequirement links, ownership, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\nverification, asset assessment, and canonical sources; validate coverage,\nunique IDs, ownership, provenance, and acyclic dependencies before allocation.\nEvery new B task must provide its context packet, output list, validation,\ncheckpoint/update procedure, collision protection, and stop condition. Do not\ncreate R-series files in this dispatcher.\n\n## Validation procedure\n\nValidate JSON, the selected chapter's 250-contract limit, unique IMP/B/R IDs,\ndependency closure and acyclicity, ownership/path collisions, allocation\nuniqueness, provenance, and asset metadata. Confirm each B owns at most seven R\nIDs and that no more than ten B tasks were created. Confirm the successor/final\naudit choice against the remaining queued chapters and ready unassigned\ncontracts. Stop and report any source conflict, missing coverage, cycle,\ncollision, unresolved authority, or need to overwrite accepted work.\n\n## Checkpoint and update procedure\n\nAtomically update the JSON and Markdown ledgers with chapter state, allocations,\ncounters, and the D0002 checkpoint only after validation. Retain reserved IDs\non repair; never renumber, replace, or rewrite an accepted B/R contract.\n\n## Collision protection\n\nBefore creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and\npath are absent from the authoritative manifest and filesystem. On collision,\nstop without overwriting or reusing the ID.\n\n## Stop condition\n\nStop immediately after at most one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and\nexactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a recursive\nprompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\n---\ntask_id: R0005\nsequence: 5\ntitle: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\ndependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\nauthoring_batch: B0004\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\nvalidator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\ncan be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\nit does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\nexpression.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\nand R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\ndependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\nAPI, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\nlocal-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or\ncache implementation.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/`.\n- `tests/content/validation.*` and deterministic content graph fixtures.\n- `docs/content-authoring.md`.\n- The versioned content-package, asset/provenance-manifest, and validator API\n  contracts.\n\nThe content registry loads only a fully validated package and is read-only at\nruntime. It does not own campaign state, save snapshots, preferences, browser\nstorage, PWA cache records, migrations, assets, or release packaging.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nModel a package with stable package ID, semantic version, schema version,\ndefault locale, scenes, exits, dialogues, quests, encounters, enemy and item\ndefinitions, rewards, localisation, and an asset/provenance manifest. Validate\nbefore registry publication: schema shape and bounded input, required fields,\nunique stable IDs, locale-key and asset/provenance references, predicates,\nscene/spawn/exit targets, reward/item/enemy references, duplicate reward IDs,\nsafe quest-item removal paths, and a reachable opening-to-ending path.\n\nValidation must return typed diagnostics and must not partially register an\ninvalid package. Build-time content import runs through this validator; derived\nbundles are never hand edited. Runtime discovery of a bad package stops the\naffected route, retains existing campaign/save data, and offers title or retry\nrather than mutating or replacing state.\n\nContent compatibility is declared explicitly so the save/recovery owner can\ncompare a snapshot's content package/version without making the content\nregistry a persistence driver. Do not checkpoint, promote, overwrite,\nquarantine, migrate, or delete a save here; those operations remain gated under\nGATE-0003 and belong to R0006 and later R0007.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and PWA use the same shared validator, schema, and read-only registry. A\nPWA cache is a delivery concern, not a content-validation result or save store;\nneither target may bypass validation, write the active package at runtime, or\nconflate cache failure with save recovery.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not create authored campaign content, dialogue, maps, art, audio, sprites,\nicons, localisation copy, release bundles, gameplay algorithms, UI flows,\nbrowser/PWA cache lifecycle, save drivers, migrations, export/import, cloud\nsync, accounts, network clients, or storage policy. Do not resolve GATE-0003\nor GATE-0004; content quantities, locales, and detail remain unapproved.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this work defines schemas and validation\nonly. Do not create, reserve, source, or generate incidental visual, audio,\nfont, icon, illustration, texture, sprite, map, dialogue, or other product\nasset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank. The schema may reserve fields for\nlater original assets and provenance review without assigning an asset.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Load a valid minimal package and prove publication succeeds only after all\n  validation phases complete.\n- Use one deterministic invalid fixture for each reference class: duplicate ID,\n  missing locale or asset/provenance record, invalid predicate, unresolved\n  scene/exit/reward/item/enemy reference, unsafe quest-item removal, and\n  unreachable ending; prove no invalid fixture is registered.\n- Traverse a valid fixture from opening scene to ending and prove required\n  transitions and rewards resolve.\n- Verify a runtime-invalid-package result retains the existing state/save and\n  provides title/retry recovery without selecting a storage API.\n- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0005, dependencies\n  match the manifest, owned paths are distinct from R0006, and every required\n  section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain validator output for the valid package and every rejected reference\nclass, reachability traversal output, registry non-publication assertions,\nruntime title/retry recovery evidence, and the pre-checkpoint loader,\nprovenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A valid minimal versioned package is the only kind of package the read-only\n  registry can publish.\n- Invalid IDs, references, predicates, localisation/provenance links, unsafe\n  quest-item removal paths, and unreachable campaign graphs fail before play.\n- Content/save compatibility is explicit while save, cache, migration, and\n  storage decisions remain separate and GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 remains retained.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-14-## Checks\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-15-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-16-- Unique, ordered B/R IDs; dependency closure/cycles; manifest output ownership;\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md:17:  requirement links; and exact, canonical provenance links.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-18-- Required R front matter (including `requirement_ids`) and matching manifest\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-19-  metadata, an explicit Asset assessment section, and verification ownership.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-20-  Missing, duplicate, blocked, unverified, and unallocated IDs are printed with\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-21-  catalogue, manifest, and specification coverage counts.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md:22:- Explicit asset assessments. Asset-required work needs unique stable `ASSET-*`\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md:23:  IDs, an asset brief, and a visual-style version; non-asset work may not reserve\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md:24:  IDs or silently introduce asset work.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-25-- Unique browser test paths and browser-impact metadata only for web/PWA\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-26-  behaviour. A web/PWA target alone does not require browser metadata.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md-27-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-1-# Runbook-authoring allocation ledger\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-2-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:3:This readable companion to [`runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](runbook-authoring-manifest.json) is the persistent allocation ledger for the mock-fantasy-quest-4 authoring system. The JSON is authoritative for IDs, provenance, dependencies, output paths, counters, and recovery state. Accepted IDs are immutable: resume from the first non-accepted batch and append only at `B0007` and `R0013`.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-4-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-5-## Dispatcher checkpoint \u2014 D0001\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-6-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-19-| 1 | B0001 | R0001 | GATE-0001; no parallel work | Record gate and R0001 ownership |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-20-| 2 | B0002 | R0002, R0003, R0010 | After B0001 | Validate seams, fixtures, tokens and retained gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-21-| 3 | B0003 | R0004, R0008 | After B0002 | Validate state slice and P0 service exclusion |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:22:| 4 | B0004 | R0005, R0006 | After B0003; R0006 waits for GATE-0003 | Validate content/save separation |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:23:| 5 | B0005 | R0007, R0009, R0011 | After B0004; R0007/GATE-0003 and R0009/GATE-0005 remain blocked | Validate migration, diagnostics, provenance |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-24-| 6 | B0006 | R0012 | After B0003 and B0004; safe in parallel with B0005 after B0004 | Cross-check foundation documentation and gates |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-25-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:26:The batches are deliberately smaller than seven where a contract is context-heavy (state, persistence, content) or tightly coupled to its predecessor. Together they form an incremental foundation vertical slice: reproducible baseline, shared seams/test harness, deterministic game state and P0 exclusion, content and recovery boundaries, then provenance/diagnostic controls and documented closure. They do not imply that the game is implemented.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-27-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:28:## Contract allocation and asset assessment\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-29-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-30-| R ID | IMP source | Writer | Output | Asset assessment |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-31-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-33-| R0002 | IMP-0002 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0002.md` | not applicable \u2014 interfaces only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-34-| R0003 | IMP-0003 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0003.md` | not applicable \u2014 deterministic fixtures only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-35-| R0004 | IMP-0004 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0004.md` | not applicable \u2014 state envelopes only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:36:| R0005 | IMP-0005 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0005.md` | not applicable \u2014 schema reserves later asset fields |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-37-| R0006 | IMP-0006 | B0004 | `runbooks/R0006.md` | not applicable \u2014 save/recovery protocol |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-38-| R0007 | IMP-0007 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0007.md` | not applicable \u2014 migrations only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-39-| R0008 | IMP-0008 | B0003 | `runbooks/R0008.md` | not applicable \u2014 negative service scope |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-40-| R0009 | IMP-0009 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0009.md` | not applicable \u2014 local diagnostics only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-41-| R0010 | IMP-0010 | B0002 | `runbooks/R0010.md` | not applicable \u2014 no final art/fonts/icons |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:42:| R0011 | IMP-0011 | B0005 | `runbooks/R0011.md` | not applicable \u2014 provenance control only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-43-| R0012 | IMP-0012 | B0006 | `runbooks/R0012.md` | not applicable \u2014 documentation only |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-44-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:45:No Wave 1 contract creates a product asset. Each contract still carries an explicit `asset_impact`, empty `asset_ids`, and an asset brief in the JSON; its author must prohibit incidental asset creation. A later asset-required contract must reserve stable product-specific IDs and a brief before assignment.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-46-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-47-## Author packet and resume rules\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-48-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:49:Each B writer receives only the baseline terminology, target constraints, templates, authoring rules, and the named specification/catalogue records in its JSON `context_packet`. Every R record has canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`, and `factory_stages` provenance. Use [`runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`](../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md) plus the F014 metadata and asset requirements.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-50-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:51:At every checkpoint, validate unique B/R IDs, output-path ownership, dependency closure, provenance, the batch maximum, asset assessment, and retained human gates. On failure, retain all assigned IDs, repair the bounded failed output, and resume that same batch. Never regenerate accepted contracts or renumber the ledger.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-52-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-53-## Queued expansion chapters\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-54-\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-64-## Structural check\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-65-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-66-```sh\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md:67:node -e 'const m=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\"); const r=m.r_contracts, b=m.batches, ids=a=>new Set(a).size===a.length; if (!ids(r.map(x=>x.id)) || !ids(b.map(x=>x.id)) || r.length!==m.expected_runbook_count || b.some(x=>x.r_contract_ids.length>7) || r.some(x=>!x.source_specifications.length || !x.source_catalogue_ids.length || !x.authoring_batch || !x.factory_stages.length || ![\"required\",\"not_applicable\"].includes(x.asset_impact) || !x.output_path || (x.asset_impact===\"required\" && (!x.asset_ids.length || !x.asset_brief))) ) process.exit(1); console.log(\"runbook authoring ledger structural check passed\")'\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md-68-```\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-6-  \"source_catalogue\": \"planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-7-  \"expected_runbook_count\": 12,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-8-  \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:9:  \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-10-  \"dispatch_history\": [\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-11-    {\"dispatcher\":\"D0001\",\"sequence\":8,\"state\":\"complete\",\"expanded_chapter\":null,\"new_imp_contract_ids\":[],\"new_authoring_batches\":[],\"ready_unassigned_contract_ids\":[],\"queued_chapters_remaining\":[\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\",\"SHARD-04\"],\"held_chapters_remaining\":[\"SHARD-05\"],\"blocking_gates\":{\"SHARD-02\":[\"GATE-0004\"],\"SHARD-03\":[\"GATE-0002\",\"GATE-0003\",\"GATE-0004\"],\"SHARD-04\":[\"GATE-0002\",\"GATE-0005\",\"GATE-0007\"],\"SHARD-05\":[\"GATE-0006\"]},\"successor_dispatcher\":\"D0002\",\"checkpoint\":\"Validated catalogue/manifest unique IMP, B, and R IDs; all 12 catalogue contracts are allocated exactly once; SHARD-02 is the first queued chapter but remains ineligible while DEC-0004/GATE-0004 is unresolved. No contract allocation, counter advance, or accepted work overwrite occurred.\"}\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-12-  ],\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-20-  \"context_packet_baseline\": {\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-21-    \"terminology\": [\"B-series = authoring runbook\", \"R-series = generated implementation runbook\", \"IMP-series = catalogue contract\", \"shared core\", \"web adapter\", \"PWA delivery adapter\", \"local save\", \"cache\", \"human gate\"],\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-22-    \"target_constraints\": [\"original offline-capable 2D single-player RPG\", \"responsive web and installable PWA\", \"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad\", \"no accounts, sync, multiplayer, purchases, or network services in P0\", \"shared core must not import platform/render/network modules\", \"PWA cache and save data remain separate\"],\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:23:    \"required_templates\": [\"runbooks/TEMPLATE.md\", \"runbooks/F014.md provenance and asset-assessment requirements\"],\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:24:    \"authoring_rules\": [\"write only assigned paths\", \"preserve gates and unanswered questions\", \"do not create incidental assets when asset_impact is not_applicable\", \"perform structural, not product-release, validation\"]\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-25-  },\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-26-  \"batches\": [\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:27:    {\"id\":\"B0001\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Bootstrap decision-gated foundation\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained inside R0001 and blocks implementation only\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0001 metadata, provenance, output ownership, explicit GATE-0001 disposition, and baseline-command evidence; batch checkpoint complete\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; author it before, not after, the gate\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:28:    {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"depends_on_batches\":[],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0001 is an implementation dependency only; R0010 retains GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0002/R0003/R0010 metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, required sections, and retained gates against the manifest\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:29:    {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0004/R0008 metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, and required sections against the manifest\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:30:    {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json:31:    {\"id\":\"B0005\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Migration, diagnostics, and provenance controls\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0006 after B0004 acceptance, except R0007 still waits for R0006\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0007 needs GATE-0003; R0009 needs GATE-0005\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0007\",\"R0009\",\"R0011\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0011\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate migration, diagnostics, and provenance fields; record unresolved gates\",\"recovery\":\"rerun only incomplete assigned IDs; preserve any accepted R contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no transport or remote diagnostics is introduced\",\"provenance review is explicit\",\"contracts remain at most three\"]},\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json-32-    {\"id\":\"B0006\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Foundation documentation closure\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0004\",\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[\"B0005 after B0004 acceptance\"],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0006 must be accepted or documented as blocked; no gate is implicitly resolved\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0012\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical